<description>
Outline every closed blue rim by painting its outside boundary red and its hole-side boundary green.

Input structure:
- The canvas background is black and all foreground pixels are blue.
- Blue pixels form one or more 4-connected objects; some objects enclose black holes.
- A hole is a 4-connected black component that does not touch the grid edge and is adjacent to exactly one blue object.

Rule:
- Leave blue pixels unchanged.
- For each hole-enclosing blue object, color edge-connected black cells red when they touch that object in the 8-neighborhood.
- Color black hole cells green when they touch their enclosing blue object in the 8-neighborhood.
- Complete the red outline at one-cell top-left diagonal closures of the filled rim.

Key insight:
- The task is not filling whole regions; it labels the two sides of each closed rim, while open blue objects have no enclosed hole and stay unchanged.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "4-connected blue objects on a black background; some objects enclose 4-connected black holes",
  "transform": "preserve blue pixels; for each object that encloses a hole, paint its outside one-cell outline red and its hole-side one-cell outline green, including diagonal corner cells; leave open objects unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 8-30 rows x 8-30 cols, black background, only blue foreground
  objects: 1-7 blue 4-connected objects; mix of rim (hole-enclosing) and distractor (open) types
  rim_objects:
    count: 0-4 per grid
    shape: irregular closed ring enclosing exactly 1 4-connected black hole; L/C-shaped rims allowed, not just rectangles
    bbox: 3-8 rows x 3-9 cols
    rim_thickness: min 1 cell, max 1-5 cells; varies within a single rim
    hole_size: 1-28 cells (4-connected)
    may_touch_grid_edge: true
  distractor_objects:
    count: 0-4 per grid; can include single-pixel objects
    shape: open blue shapes that do NOT enclose any 4-connected black hole; ring-like with gap or irregular polyomino
    size: 1-29 cells
  separation: all blue objects pairwise Chebyshev distance >= 2; rim objects >= 3 from any other object [observed]
  blue_density: 13-28% of grid cells [observed]
  transform:
    blue_pixels: unchanged
    red: for each rim object, paint edge-connected black cells that are 8-adjacent to the rim; also cap 1-cell top-left diagonal closures
    green: for each rim object, paint hole cells that are 8-adjacent to the rim
    distractors: unchanged (no red/green added)
generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size 8-30 x 8-30; choose N_rim in 0-4 and N_dist in 0-4 (total objects 1-7, at least 1 rim or 1 distractor)
    2. For each rim object, build an irregular closed ring on a local canvas; start with a filled convex-ish blob (3-8 x 3-9 bbox), then carve out a connected interior hole leaving >= 1 cell rim thickness everywhere
    3. For each distractor, build an open shape (polyomino that does not enclose a 4-connected hole); e.g. random-walk or L/U/C shape
    4. Place all objects on the grid with Chebyshev separation >= 3 between any rim and any other object (>= 2 between distractors); rim objects may overlap the grid edge
    5. Verify no spurious holes exist (all black components except the intended holes are edge-connected)
```
